Package: riscos-kernel-wdk2023
Architecture: arm64
Maintainer: Andrew Youll <adyoull@users.noreply.github.com>
Depends: riscos-support (>= 1.0.0001-1)
Conflicts: riscos-kernel-generic
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-rolpkg
Description: Linux 7.2 kernel for RISC OS on Linux on the Windows Dev Kit 2023
 The Linux kernel the Windows Dev Kit 2023 (Snapdragon 8cx Gen 3, "Project
 Volterra") starts from the card's EFI partition (EFI/BOOT/BOOTAA64.EFI,
 which loads blackrock.dtb), with that device tree. Installing it copies
 them onto the EFI partition, keeping the old ones as *.old; a restart
 starts the new kernel.
